    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d995">

                <pb facs="1037" n="1025" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.76/10–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sands</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-13T13:00:00+03:06">October 13, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 13—12:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>378. When asked again for reply to Department’s telegram 289, September 25<anchor
                        n="28" xml:id="d995-f1"/> Acting Foreign Minister said matter was “under
                    consideration” <pb facs="1038" n="1026" xml:id="pg1026"/> and reverted to
                    suggestion that we “settle it between ourselves and Britain”. He admitted as
                    well strong British pressure against bilateral air rights agreement.<anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d995-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sands</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d995-f1" n="28" xml:id="d995-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it advised that the Mackay Radio and Telegraph Company had inquired
                    about the present status of its proposal to build a radio station for the Saudi
                    Arabian Government (890F.76/9–2545).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d995-f2" n="29" xml:id="d995-f2-content">
                <p>For documentation on the proposal of the United States to enter a civil air
                    transport agreement with Saudi Arabia, see <ref target="#pg845">pp. 845</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
